    core: `Ceres, the principle of nurturance and cycles of care, and Venus, love, aesthetic value, and relational warmth, are in the same elemental family, separated by 120 degrees of natural resonance. The trine means the capacity to care and the capacity to love speak the same language. This person can express affection through tending and can also create relational beauty. Care and love are not in conflict. They are recognized as parts of the same relational expression.`,
    behavioral: `The relationship between caring and loving is collaborative. This person's affection is expressed through sustained attention, and that attention feels beautiful rather than burdensome. The capacity to tend is genuine and creates relational warmth rather than depleting it. The behavioral signature is graceful caregiving. The person loves by creating conditions for beauty and growth, and the labor of that creation is integrated into the pleasure of the relationship. The trine allows care to operate as an expression of love rather than as a separate obligation.`,
